<http://data.silknow.org/object/bc1a21fa-73a0-30f9-8685-bc8ef5ea5bc4/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Towel or napkin, linen embroidered with silk in double darning on the diagonal and satin stitch, and with metal thread in double darning on the diagonal, fishbone and counted satin stitch.       \nThe borders are worked predominantly in metal thread which forms a narrow band along the upper and lower edge.  Each border contains three motifs in which six leaves (five metal thread and one pink silk) branch from one side of a vertical stem; small leaves are worked  in blue silk."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/bc1a21fa-73a0-30f9-8685-bc8ef5ea5bc4> .

